@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="wizard">
    <div class="wizard-card">
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p class="wizard-hint">
            Re-Waste is a student project. This page says what we keep and what we do not.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">When you use the wizard</h2>
        <p>
            You do not need an account to get a recommendation. Your answers are held only for your visit.
            Nothing is stored in our database unless you log in and press <strong>Save this result</strong>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What we keep when you save a result</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>The phone's brand and model</li>
            <li>Its age in years and its condition</li>
            <li>Whether it holds personal data</li>
            <li>Whether its battery is damaged</li>
            <li>The first part of your postcode, for example EH1</li>
            <li>The recommended routes (up to three) and the reason for each</li>
            <li>The date and time you saved it, linked to your account</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What we do not keep</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Your full postcode. Only the first part is saved.</li>
            <li>Any other answers. If a question is not in the list above, it is not saved.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your account</h2>
        <p>
            Your account holds your name, your email address and, if you add one, your phone number.
            Your password is stored in scrambled form, never as plain text.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Who can see your saved results</h2>
        <p>
            Only you, when you are logged in. Nobody else who logs in can open or delete them.
            The site manager can see how many results have been saved, but not who saved them or what they say.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Deleting your data</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>One result:</strong> open <a asp-controller="MyDevices" asp-action="Index">My devices</a> and choose Delete.</li>
            <li><strong>Everything:</strong> click your name at the top, choose Personal data, then Delete. This removes your account and all your saved results.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>